@{ ViewData["Title"] = "How it works"; }
<section class="section" style="padding-top:40px"><div class="container" style="max-width:860px">
    <h1 style="font-size:34px">How RiseUp works</h1>
    <div class="card card-b mt16"><h3>Requests and the 14-day window</h3><ul class="small">
        <li>Only one pending request — pitch <em>or</em> invitation — can exist between a startup and an investor at a time.</li>
        <li>Unanswered requests expire exactly 14 days after they were sent. After expiry you can send a new one immediately.</li>
        <li>If a request is declined early, a new one can be sent only once 14 days have passed since the <em>original</em> send time.</li>
        <li>Accepting creates exactly one connection and one private group chat. Connections cannot be closed, but chats can be muted.</li></ul></div>
    <div class="card card-b mt16"><h3>Tokens (founders)</h3><ul class="small">
        <li>20 one-time Welcome tokens on first successful verification — pitch use only, never expire.</li>
        <li>Purchased tokens never expire and can be used for pitches and post promotions.</li>
        <li>A delivered pitch costs 1 token (Welcome first). Rejected or undeliverable pitches cost nothing.</li></ul></div>
    <div class="card card-b mt16"><h3>Invitations (investors)</h3><ul class="small"><li>Free. Up to 10 successful invitations per calendar day, Asia/Dhaka time, reset at midnight with no carry-over.</li></ul></div>
    <div class="card card-b mt16"><h3>Where AI is used — and where it is not</h3><ul class="small">
        <li><strong>Model 1</strong> approves or rejects new or edited posts and founder pitches. It never writes or rewrites your text.</li>
        <li><strong>Model 2</strong> ranks matches and targets promoted posts, with automatic rule-based fallback.</li>
        <li>AI never verifies documents, reads private chats or comments, sends requests, or spends tokens.</li></ul></div>
</div></section>
